menu "Tab5 battery"

    config MQJS_TAB5_BATTERY
        bool "Enable Tab5 battery monitoring, charge control and protection"
        default n
        depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32P4
        help
            M5Stack Tab5 battery support: INA226 monitoring (0x41, internal
            I2C bus), charge enable / quick-charge selection through the
            PI4IOE5V6408 expander at 0x44, a coulomb-counting fuel gauge with
            IR compensation, and the load-shed / over-discharge ladder that
            shuts the device down before the pack's 6.0 V protection latches
            (recovering from that needs the battery physically removed).

            Off by default so Stamp-P4 builds are unaffected; when disabled
            pwr_tab5.h provides no-op inline stubs.

            NOTE: without this, a Tab5 never charges. The charger is gated by
            a firmware-driven pin and the device only charges while powered
            on, so a build with this option off drains the pack even on USB.

    config MQJS_TAB5_BATTERY_INVERT_CURRENT
        bool "INA226 current is negative while charging"
        depends on MQJS_TAB5_BATTERY
        default n
        help
            The INA226's orientation on this board is not documented; the
            factory UI treats "current >= 0" as charging and this default
            follows it. Set this if the device reports a discharge while it
            is visibly charging. Also settable at runtime with
            pwr_tab5_set_current_sign(-1) / power.sign(-1) during bring-up,
            so a probe run does not need a reflash.

    config MQJS_TAB5_BATTERY_GRACE_S
        int "Seconds between the shutdown warning and cutting power"
        depends on MQJS_TAB5_BATTERY
        range 5 120
        default 30
        help
            When the pack reaches the shutdown tier, apps are told through
            sys.onStop("battery") and the countdown starts. Power is cut on
            the acknowledgement or when this expires, whichever comes first.
            A charger appearing during the countdown aborts it.

endmenu
